    "title": "Reconstruct Itinerary",
    "workload": "build a 1000-edge Eulerian graph once (40 cycles through JFK over ~961 airports), then 250 punches; each punch re-runs the full Hierholzer pass -- adjacency build, per-airport destination sort, recursive walk, reverse -- reading tickets from a rotated offset so the call cannot be hoisted while the sorted destinations keep the itinerary invariant; sink=position-weighted checksum of the route. NOTE: kara's adjacency build is O(degree) per edge because m[k].push(x) is rejected by codegen (ledger B-2026-07-25-5); the other four use their O(1) idiom.",
